            For context, many mainstream whey proteins land somewhere around $1 to $1.50 per 25 g of protein at full retail, and a complete protein gives more muscle-building value for each of those grams. So per gram, Vital Proteins is roughly twice the price of ordinary whey while doing less for muscle. That is not a scandal; it is what you pay for a specialty ingredient that most people buy for skin and joints rather than for protein.
          </p>

          <p>
            Fortune rated its value 1 out of 5 while scoring the product highly on everything else, and that matches what the arithmetic shows. If you take collagen daily, the larger tub saves about 17 percent per gram over the small one, and stick packs are the most expensive way to buy it. Our <a href="/best-collagen-protein-powder/">best collagen protein powder</a> ranking compares Vital Proteins with cheaper and certified alternatives on the same per-gram basis.
